From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hotschmoe <isaac@mass-engineering.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 03:11:10 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: cix: sky1: name the GPT clocks "apb" and "func"

timer-sky1-gpt asks for the clocks "apb" and "func" and tries the ACPI
names (fch_timer_apb_clk, fch_timer_func_clk) only on an ACPI system. The
gpt_timer nodes use the ACPI names, so on a device-tree boot the probe of
gpt_timer3 fails:

  sky1_timer 4116000.gpt_timer: error -ENOENT: failed to get func clock

and tick broadcast falls back to bc_hrtimer. Both CPU idle states below
WFI are local-timer-stop, and the CPU that holds the broadcast hrtimer may
enter neither, so one CPU is always in WFI and the cluster never reaches
cluster-sleep.

Use the names the driver asks for.

Tested on a Minisforum MS-R1 (device tree based on sky1-orion-o6.dts) with
the same clock-names set on gpt_timer3: "Sky1 GPT timer initialized at
25000000 Hz", broadcast device sky1_timer, and at an idle login screen
all twelve CPUs are in cluster-sleep together 90% of the time (0% before).

Signed-off-by: hotschmoe <isaac@mass-engineering.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/cix/sky1.dtsi | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/cix/sky1.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/cix/sky1.dtsi
index a170057fd..2bd3ad8bf 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/cix/sky1.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/cix/sky1.dtsi
@@ -3121,7 +3121,7 @@ gpt_timer0: gpt_timer@04110000 {
 			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 467 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>;
 			clocks = <&scmi_clk CLK_TREE_FCH_TIMER_APB>,
 						<&scmi_clk CLK_TREE_FCH_TIMER_FUN>;
-			clock-names = "fch_timer_apb_clk", "fch_timer_func_clk";
+			clock-names = "apb", "func";
 			resets = <&src_fch SW_TIMER_RST_FUNC_N>;
 			reset-names = "func_reset";
 			status = "disabled";
@@ -3133,7 +3133,7 @@ gpt_timer1: gpt_timer@04112000 {
 			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 468 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>;
 			clocks = <&scmi_clk CLK_TREE_FCH_TIMER_APB>,
 						<&scmi_clk CLK_TREE_FCH_TIMER_FUN>;
-			clock-names = "fch_timer_apb_clk", "fch_timer_func_clk";
+			clock-names = "apb", "func";
 			resets = <&src_fch SW_TIMER_RST_FUNC_N>;
 			reset-names = "func_reset";
 			status = "disabled";
@@ -3145,7 +3145,7 @@ gpt_timer2: gpt_timer@04114000 {
 			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 469 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>;
 			clocks = <&scmi_clk CLK_TREE_FCH_TIMER_APB>,
 						<&scmi_clk CLK_TREE_FCH_TIMER_FUN>;
-			clock-names = "fch_timer_apb_clk", "fch_timer_func_clk";
+			clock-names = "apb", "func";
 			resets = <&src_fch SW_TIMER_RST_FUNC_N>;
 			reset-names = "func_reset";
 			status = "disabled";
@@ -3157,7 +3157,7 @@ gpt_timer3: gpt_timer@04116000 {
 			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 470 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>;
 			clocks = <&scmi_clk CLK_TREE_FCH_TIMER_APB>,
 						<&scmi_clk CLK_TREE_FCH_TIMER_FUN>;
-			clock-names = "fch_timer_apb_clk", "fch_timer_func_clk";
+			clock-names = "apb", "func";
 			resets = <&src_fch SW_TIMER_RST_FUNC_N>;
 			reset-names = "func_reset";
 			status = "okay";
